## Project Structure

- Routes live in `src/app`
  - Root (game) page live in `src/app/(game)`
  - Other routes live in `src/app/(pages)`
  - auth pages `src/app/login` and `src/app/signup`

- Feature components live in `src/components/`
- Reusable UI parts live in `src/components/ui/`
- Component folder structure: `ComponentName/index.tsx` + `styles.module.scss`
- Utils: One file per function in `src/utils/` with barrel export via `index.ts`
- SEO utilities: `src/utils/seo/`
- Constants: `src/constants/`
- Hooks: `src/hooks/` with brief JSDoc comments

## Code Style

- Files should not exceed ~100 lines. If larger, split into:
  - Utility functions in `src/utils/`
  - Custom hooks in `src/hooks/`
  - Smaller components
- One React component per file
- Extract complex logic from components into hooks or utils
- Components: use arrow functions and declare `export default` at the end
- Hooks: use named exports, e.g. `export function useSomething()`
- Prefer `classnames/bind` when combining classes or using prop-based classes
- Prefer `type Props` for local component/hook props, and `ComponentNameProps` when exported
- Prefer `PropsWithChildren` over `children: ReactNode` unless explicit ReactNode is needed
- Prefer `props: Props` param and destructure props on the first line, except when no props are used
- Prefer single quotes in JS/TS/TSX
- Omit empty returns: use `return undefined` in functions and `return null` in React components

## SEO

- Use `generateMetadata()` from `src/utils/seo` for all page metadata
- Hidden pages: add to `HIDDEN_ROUTES` in `middleware.ts` + set `noIndex: true`
- Public pages: add to `PUBLIC_PAGES` in `src/utils/seo/publicPages.ts`
- Production URL: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` env variable

## Next.js

- App Router in `src/app/`
- Route groups: `(pages)` for content pages
- Dynamic game: `[[...slug]]/` with client-only rendering
